<% layout("layouts/boilerplate") -%>

<div class="container my-5">
  <div class="row justify-content-center">
    <div class="col-lg-9 col-12">
      <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm rounded-4 p-4 p-md-5">
        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-file-contract text-danger me-2"></i>Terms of Service</h2>
        <p class="text-muted small">Last updated: November 2026</p>
        <hr class="my-4">

        <h5 class="fw-bold">1. Agreement to Terms</h5>
        <p class="text-secondary">By accessing or using Wanderlust, you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree to all terms and conditions, do not access or use the platform.</p>

        <h5 class="fw-bold mt-4">2. Host Obligations</h5>
        <p class="text-secondary">Hosts are responsible for the accuracy of their listings, pricing, and availability. All property descriptions, photos, and amenities must reflect the true state of the accommodation.</p>

        <h5 class="fw-bold mt-4">3. Bookings and Cancellations</h5>
        <p class="text-secondary">Guests may reserve stays based on confirmed availability. Double bookings are prevented programmatically by the server. Cancellations and refunds are handled in accordance with the listing's cancellation policy.</p>

        <h5 class="fw-bold mt-4">4. Verified Reviews</h5>
        <p class="text-secondary">Reviews can only be submitted by registered guests who have completed a confirmed stay at the property. Spurious, abusive, or false reviews are strictly prohibited.</p>

        <h5 class="fw-bold mt-4">5. Limitation of Liability</h5>
        <p class="text-secondary">Wanderlust connects hosts and guests. While we strive to maintain high service quality, we are not responsible for direct host-guest disputes outside platform functionality.</p>

        <div class="mt-4">
          <a href="/listings" class="btn btn-outline-danger rounded-pill px-4"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left me-2"></i>Back to Explore</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
